---
title: Everyday loaf
servings: 12
tags: [baking, bread, make-ahead]
source: Invented for this repository
notes: >-
  An overnight rise in the fridge. Mix on a Saturday evening, bake Sunday
  morning.
---

Mix the @bread flour{500%g}, @water{350%ml}, @fine salt{10%g} and
@instant yeast{3%g} in a #large bowl{} until no dry flour remains. Cover and
leave ~{30%minutes}.

Fold the dough over on itself four times in the bowl. Repeat three more times at
~{30%minute} intervals.

Cover and refrigerate ~{12%hours}.

Shape into a round on a floured surface and leave to rise ~{2%hours} at room
temperature, seam down in a #banneton{}.

Heat the oven and a #cast-iron pot{} to 250°C. Turn the loaf in, score it, and
bake covered ~{20%minutes}, then uncovered ~{20%minutes} at 220°C.

Cool completely on a rack before cutting — at least ~{1%hour}.
